d RootedFileSystemProvider and SftpFileSystemProviderFacade instances. After reverting that unsuccessful repair, the exact finalization command passed current-defaults but failed future-defaults because sun.nio.fs.LinuxFileSystemProvider also requires prohibited build-time initialization; see forge/logs/org.apache.sshd:sshd-sftp:2.18.0/local-review-finalization/review_future-defaults_latest_GraalVM_test-2026-09-10T07-12-43-936009Z.log. No compliant contribution-local repair was established, the evidence does not prove a shared repository defect, and §FS-contribution-contract.5.4 is not established, so §FS-contribution-contract.5.5 applies.\\n./stats/org.apache.sshd/sshd-sftp/2.18.0/forge-publication.json:60:    \\\"finding_body\\\": \\\"The coordinate's build.gradle adds --initialize-at-build-time for Apache SSHD and SLF4J classes. This violates §FS-test-contract.2.7, which permits only --add-opens/--add-exports native configuration in a test build. I removed the flag and preserved all three scenarios while replacing the rooted server filesystem with SSHD's native filesystem, but the current-defaults lane still failed because Native Image embedded service-discovered RootedFileSystemProvider and SftpFileSystemProviderFacade instances. After reverting that unsuccessful repair, the exact finalization command passed current-defaults but failed future-defaults because sun.nio.fs.LinuxFileSystemProvider also requires prohibited build-time initialization; see forge/logs/org.apache.sshd:sshd-sftp:2.18.0/local-review-finalization/review_future-defaults_latest_GraalVM_test-2026-09-10T07-12-43-936009Z.log. No compliant contribution-local repair was established, the evidence does not prove a shared repository defect, and §FS-contribution-contract.5.4 is not established, so §FS-contribution-contract.5.5 applies.\\\",\\n./tests/src/org.osgi/core/4.3.0/build.gradle:22:                    '--initialize-at-run-time=org.osgi.framework.CapabilityPermissionCollection')\\n./tests/src/org.osgi/core/4.3.0/build.gradle:24:                    '--initialize-at-run-time=org.osgi.framework.PackagePermissionCollection')\\n./tests/src/org.osgi/core/4.3.0/build.gradle:26:                    '--initialize-at-run-time=org.osgi.framework.ServicePermissionCollection')\\n./tests/src/org.osgi/org.osgi.core/4.3.0/build.gradle:21:            buildArgs.add('--initialize-at-run-time=org.osgi.framework.AdaptPermissionCollection')\\n./tests/src/org.osgi/org.osgi.core/4.3.0/build.gradle:22:            buildArgs.add('--initialize-at-run-time=org.osgi.framework.AdminPermissionCollection')\\n./tests/src/tomcat/jasper-runtime/5.5.23/build.gradle:31:            buildArgs.add(\\\"--initialize-at-run-time=org.apache.jasper.security.SecurityClassLoad\\\")\\n./tests/src/org.osgi/org.osgi.core/4.3.1/build.gradle:21:            buildArgs.add('--initialize-at-run-time=org.osgi.framework.AdaptPermissionCollection')\\n./tests/src/org.osgi/org.osgi.core/4.3.1/build.gradle:22:            buildArgs.add('--initialize-at-run-time=org.osgi.framework.AdminPermissionCollection')\\n./tests/src/com.opencsv/opencsv/5.6/build.gradle:34:            buildArgs(\\\"--initialize-at-build-time=${nonDecimalNumberFormatProvider}\\\")\\n./stats/com.azure/azure-identity/1.18.0/execution-metrics.json:57:        \\\"msal4j and azure-core-http-netty are new transitive surfaces for this repo (no existing metadata) and native-image builds may need iterative --initialize-at-build-time fixes similar to those already applied for azure-core-http-jdk-httpclient; this should be handled by the normal generate/fix workflow rather than pre-declared here.\\\"\\n./tests/src/org.rxtx/rxtx/2.1.7/build.gradle:62:            buildArgs.add(\\\"--initialize-at-run-time=gnu.io.CommPortIdentifier,gnu.io.RXTXCommDriver,gnu.io.RXTXVersion\\\")\\n./stats/io.micrometer/micrometer-registry-statsd/1.16.5/execution-metrics.json:17:      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"All Netty/reactor-netty/JCTools classes referenced by the issue are shaded inside micrometer-registry-statsd itself (no separate dependency exists to add). Testing needs no Docker StatsD server or env vars — StatsdConfig.host()/port() can point at a local DatagramSocket. The real work is native-image metadata (initialize-at-run-time + reflection) for the shaded classes, which is the normal generation/fix workflow, not extra setup.\\\",\\n./stats/io.micrometer/micrometer-registry-statsd/1.16.5/execution-metrics.json:19:      \\\"agent_guidance\\\": \\\"Exercise StatsdMeterRegistry with a plain java.net.DatagramSocket bound to localhost on an ephemeral port as the 'StatsD server' (set via StatsdConfig.host()/port()) instead of a real StatsD/Datadog agent or Docker container — the wire protocol is just UDP text lines. Since publishing is async, poll/await the socket receive with a timeout rather than sleeping a fixed duration, and always call registry.close() in a finally block to stop the shaded reactor-netty client and avoid hanging the test JVM. When investigating the reported native-image bug, note the jar already bundles META-INF/native-image config for io.netty/io.projectreactor under their real (unshaded) coordinates — the gap is that the shaded class names (io.micrometer.shaded.io.netty.*, io.micrometer.shaded.io.netty.util.internal.shaded.org.jctools.*) aren't covered, matching the initialize-at-run-time and reflection metadata listed in the issue (DNS resolver holders, epoll/unix transport classes, JCTools MPSC queue field-offset classes). Confirm exact `initialize-at-run-time` needs by running native-image-agent trace plus fixTestNativeImageRun rather than copying the issue's list verbatim, since it was captured against a different Micrometer/Netty pairing (Micronaut, not this repo's harness).\\\",\\n./stats/io.micrometer/micrometer-registry-statsd/1.16.5/execution-metrics.json:105:      \\\"agent_guidance\\\": \\\"Exercise StatsdMeterRegistry with a plain java.net.DatagramSocket bound to localhost on an ephemeral port as the 'StatsD server' (set via StatsdConfig.host()/port()) instead of a real StatsD/Datadog agent or Docker container — the wire protocol is just UDP text lines. Since publishing is async, poll/await the socket receive with a timeout rather than sleeping a fixed duration, and always call registry.close() in a finally block to stop the shaded reactor-netty client and avoid hanging the test JVM. When investigating the reported native-image bug, note the jar already bundles META-INF/native-image config for io.netty/io.projectreactor under their real (unshaded) coordinates — the gap is that the shaded class names (io.micrometer.shaded.io.netty.*, io.micrometer.shaded.io.netty.util.internal.shaded.org.jctools.*) aren't covered, matching the initialize-at-run-time and reflection metadata listed in the issue (DNS resolver holders, epoll/unix transport classes, JCTools MPSC queue field-offset classes). Confirm exact `initialize-at-run-time` needs by running native-image-agent trace plus fixTestNativeImageRun rather than copying the issue's list verbatim, since it was captured against a different Micrometer/Netty pairing (Micronaut, not this repo's harness).\\\",\\n./stats/io.micrometer/micrometer-registry-statsd/1.16.5/execution-metrics.json:129:      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"All Netty/reactor-netty/JCTools classes referenced by the issue are shaded inside micrometer-registry-statsd itself (no separate dependency exists to add). Testing needs no Docker StatsD server or env vars — StatsdConfig.host()/port() can point at a local DatagramSocket. The real work is native-image metadata (initialize-at-run-time + reflection) for the shaded classes, which is the normal generation/fix workflow, not extra setup.\\\"\\n./stats/org.jetbrains.kotlin/kotlin-stdlib/1.7.10/execution-metrics.json:54:      \\\"agent_guidance\\\": \\\"Use in-process Kotlin/JVM tests against public stdlib APIs and preserve the existing --initialize-at-build-time=kotlin.Metadata Native Image argument. The existing kotlinx-corouti